  "metadata": {
    "title": "Projectile Motion: Fixed Speed, Changing Angle",
    "subject": "Physics",
    "objective": "Show how launch angle changes the trajectory at a fixed speed.",
    "learner": "Knows speed and vectors informally.",
    "misconceptions": [
      "45 degrees always gives the maximum range regardless of launch height",
      "Horizontal speed changes the vertical acceleration"
    ],
    "expectedUnderstanding": [
      "A fixed-speed projectile follows a parabola whose height and range change with launch angle.",
      "At equal launch and landing heights, 45 degrees gives the maximum range.",
      "The vertical acceleration is independent of the horizontal speed.",
      "Supplementary launch angles can produce the same range with different maximum heights."
    ]
  },
